This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, PowerShell, Read, Skill, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__get_issue, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__list_comments, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_comment, mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_issue, mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request, mcp__t3-code__preview_evaluate, mcp__t3-code__preview_open, mcp__t3-code__preview_resize, mcp__t3-code__preview_snapshot</tools-used-before-summary>
Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent**

   **Original `/goal`** (resumed; treat it as the directive and don't pause to ask):
   > "Own the inkling UI refactor end to end: SQU-124 (tracker) and SQU-125 to SQU-132. Work until all are done; don't pause between layers. Read AGENTS.md (binding). Before starting any issue, read its description and every comment on it. The comments are newer and win wherever they differ from the description. SQU-124's "Brief" comment holds the rules for every layer (gate, mechanics, comments, tests, verify, stop, done); re-read it at each layer. Gate: #131 and #171 merged into main, and a clean worktree. Otherwise report and stop. Order: SQU-125 branches off main, any time. Then 126 → 132, each branched from and PR'd against the previous; 126 targets main. You have standing approval to open these PRs as drafts; mark each ready once it's verified and `bun run check` is green. Never: change visible behavior without sign-off, fork the glass Surface, put glass or Base UI in grid cards, regress #174's data path or App()'s ordering guarantees, or wait on sleeps. Report briefly at each PR. Finish with a summary comment on SQU-124."

   #131 and #171 were closed unmerged; we proceeded as if the gate was lifted.

   **SQU-124 Brief (re-read this layer)**
   - Parity port only. Keep #174's data path. Glass sparingly, never on grid cards. No Zustand or TanStack Query.
   - Comments: default to none, at most four lines. Keep only race/ordering, security, platform quirks, or cross-file invariants. Lint directives and license headers stay.
   - Tests: moved tests stay unchanged; new tests must meet SQU-132's keep bar. No sleeps, timeouts, retries, wall-clock deltas, polling or skips.
   - Verify:
     - Each PR lists the "Hit every surface" entries that applied.
     - Check the full app via verify-inkling (liquid) and preview (CSS fallback).
     - Before/after screenshots, base vs branch.
     - Keyboard and focus return for every Dialog, Tabs and Menu.
   - `bun run check` once per layer (this overrides AGENTS.md's "no repo-wide checks").
   - Draft PRs are pre-approved; mark ready when verified and green.
   - Rebase upper layers if a lower one changes. Never force-push others' branches.
   - Changelog only where its rules ask; SQU-132 owns the final rewrite.
   - Stop and ask only if:
     - the gate fails;
     - an AGENTS.md rule fights the work;
     - a change alters visible behavior beyond parity;
     - Base UI can't coexist with the glass canvas;
     - something is destructive or touches the live library;
     - CI is red for an unpinnable reason.
   - Done when:
     - every child PR is green, linked, and its issue is In Review;
     - App.css is gone, and no god files remain;
     - storage.mjs is split;
     - AGENTS.md has the comment and test rules;
     - docs match reality;
     - a summary comment on SQU-124 lists every PR, test and comment counts before/after, anything skipped, and follow-ups.

   **SQU-128 description**
   - Extract the capture bar (search field, filter row, pinned query row, capture error), the capture modal and the shortcuts modal into `src/features/capture/`.
   - Build `Dialog` and `SearchField` primitives on Base UI, restyled with Tailwind; delete the matching App.css blocks.
   - Every entry point behaves the same: Add button, paste, drag and drop, clipboard, screenshot and deep link.
   - Done when:
     - capture stays instant;
     - search stays instant with the debounce unchanged;
     - Dialog gives a focus trap, Escape and focus return;
     - the SQU-120 native folder-picker race stays fixed (modals still respond after the picker closes);
     - the mascot's search-eyes and focus behavior are unchanged;
     - before/after images, checked in the full app.

   **SQU-128 comment (wins over the description):**
   > "Add now opens in place into a menu (`components/AddMenu/`), which is likely the first Menu consumer. It is vendored: its LICENSE.md and attribution move with it and feed the licenses page. When idle, search is a small pill showing the current view. It grows into the full bar on focus and shrinks back on Escape. Keep both, along with the mascot's search-eyes. Tooltips over `.capture-bar` render as liquid glass (see SQU-126)."

   **Remaining scopes (from the earlier summary)**
   - **SQU-129:**
     - library grid, cards, list and filters go to `features/library`;
     - cards stay plain; ItemMedia stays the single thumbnail logic;
     - run `scripts/bench-library-grid.mjs` before and after;
     - GradualBlur (keep its LICENSE) plus LibraryEdgeFade;
     - view dock;
     - card ContextMenu on Menu, with the popup outside the card;
     - keep canvasImageCrossOrigin;
     - video posters, with no `<video>` in the grid;
     - no full-list reloads.
   - **SQU-130:**
     - Settings and Archive go to `features/settings`;
     - Tabs, Switch and form primitives;
     - Settings reopens on Library, and the cached size shows at once;
     - optional facts stay hidden when unavailable;
     - Archive reverse states keep working;
     - Licenses and Appearance tabs; LicenseFilter on Menu;
     - windowing stays intact;
     - the Archive count gap is known; don't fix it.
   - **SQU-131:**
     - split ExpandedItemOverlay into `features/item-view`;
     - grows from the card onto a dotted stage, inspector on the right;
     - closes only from Close or Escape;
     - the note editor keeps full height;
     - keep canvasImageCrossOrigin;
     - zoom and pan unchanged; no shadow on the scaled image;
     - Space chips use live membership with no stale rollback;
     - lazy chunks are warmed; every kind opens;
     - the mascot sits in the inspector corner;
     - PdfViewer onto Dialog if it fits.
   - **SQU-132:**
     - delete App.css (reader.css stays);
     - no UI file over about 600 lines without a reason;
     - docs: tech-stack styling, design.md tokens, a changelog line under Changed referencing SQU-124;
     - update t3.json, knip and biome if needed;
     - test prune with before/after counts and bun test time;
     - AGENTS.md rules.
   - **SQU-132 keep bar:**
     - Keep: extraction/sanitizing, embed allowlists, OCR scoring, queue leases/recovery, migrations/persistence, asset path containment/range, deep link and external-format parsing, ordering/race guarantees, liquidGlassShape, and regression tests.
     - Delete: type-redundant, trivial, DOM-basic, static markup, mock mirrors, smoke, duplicate rows, and wall-clock tests.

   **AGENTS.md safety constraints (verbatim essentials)**
   - "Never `pkill -f`, `pgrep | kill`, or `kill` a PID you found by matching a name, path, or worktree string... Kill only a PID you captured at spawn, or the owner of your port after confirming it is your worktree (`Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort <port> -State Listen` and the `Win32_Process` command line on Windows)."
   - "Never start a server against [the live library], never open it read-write, never clean it up."
   - "Never hardcode a localhost port, an absolute user path, or a machine specific model cache path into source or committed config."
   - "Never commit a database file, a model artifact, a downloaded embedding, or a benchmark output besides the two tracked files. Never commit a pairing secret, token, or full capture URL with real content."
   - "Never `Start-Sleep` (or any blocking wait) after launching a server."
   - No calls home or analytics.
   - Don't commit plans or scratch; keep scratch outside the worktree. Never commit PR-only screenshots (upload them to GitHub).
   - PR body: Linear link at the top, then the problem and fix, ending with model and harness. UI changes need before/after images.
   - Linear: move the issue to In Progress, post progress comments, never rewrite descriptions, link the PR, move it to In Review.
   - Commits end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. PR bodies end with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.
   - Never use bare `git stash`. Register every PR with `mcp__t3-code__link_pull_request`.
   - Entire hook: never create checkpoints by hand; leave setup and destructive entire commands to the user.

2. **Key Technical Concepts**
   - **Stack:** Electron, React 19, Vite 8, Tailwind v4 (layers `theme, base, components, utilities`, no preflight), Base UI 1.9.0 (Dialog with Root/Portal/Backdrop/Viewport/Popup, plus Input and Button), motion/react, Biome, knip, tsc-rs, Bun 1.4.2.
   - **Cascade:**
     - App.css and `src/ui/Surface.css` are **unlayered**, so they beat Tailwind utilities.
     - Surface.css loads after App.css: nothing imported before App.css pulls in Surface.
     - On main the expanded search bar had the deep shadow under CSS glass, and none under liquid glass (`.glass[data-liquid]{box-shadow:none}` wins on source order).
     - The global `button/input:focus-visible` outline in App.css is unlayered, so utilities that change outlines need `!`.
   - **Tailwind specifics:**
     - `wide` breakpoint is 781px; `max-wide:` matches the old `max-width:780px`.
     - Conflicting utilities in one class list resolve by Tailwind's sort order, not class order, so never include both.
     - Arbitrary properties are used for exactness (`[translate:-50%_-50%]`, `[transform:...]`).
   - **Base UI Dialog:**
     - `initialFocus` takes a ref.
     - The default `finalFocus` returns focus to the trigger or the previously focused element.
     - Transitions use `data-starting-style` / `data-ending-style`.
     - It handles Escape, the focus trap and outside press.
   - **Scratch tooling:**
     - In `%TEMP%\squ126`: `cdp.ts`, `diff.ts` (pixel diff), `styles.ts` (computed-style dump, CDP 9400, 960×540, takes url/root/setup/appearance).
     - In `%TEMP%\squ127`:
       - `flow.ts` (preview flow) and `appflow.ts` (full app);
       - `rerun.sh <name> <port> <repo> <out>` (cleanup, `launch.mjs`, then run `appflow`);
       - `launch.mjs` mirrors instance.mjs and adds `--disable-backgrounding-occluded-windows --disable-renderer-backgrounding --disable-background-timer-throttling`;
       - `probe.ts`, `shot.ts`, `nav.ts`, `db.ts` (readonly bun:sqlite), `sbs.ts`, `crop.ts`.
     - Note: `c.until` wraps `Boolean(expr)`, so a Promise expression is always truthy.
   - **PR evidence** is uploaded to the `pr-evidence-mascot` release: `gh release upload pr-evidence-mascot *.png -R Squidys-Tools/inkling --clobber`. URLs follow `https://github.com/Squidys-Tools/inkling/releases/download/pr-evidence-mascot/<name>.png`.
   - **Entire Gates** on PRs needs human approval and is pending while the PR is a draft. CI checks plus "Findings passed" count as green for us.
   - **`bun run check`** stops at `bun test`, which has 2 known Windows-only baseline fails (portable-path precedence, capture-server EBUSY). Run the remaining steps separately: `knip`, `lint`, `build`, `build:app`, `ingest:smoke`, `--cwd extension build`.
   - **Lint baseline:** CRLF `.d.mts` files (`electron/ocr.d.mts`, `electron/pdf.d.mts`, `scripts/third-party-licenses/collect.d.mts`, `src/lib/deepLinkCore.d.mts`) plus the `noUselessFragments` info in App.tsx.
   - **CRLF in the working tree** for tracked LF files: fix by deleting the files and running `git checkout --` them, after confirming `git diff --quiet`.

3. **Files and Code Sections**

   **SQU-127 (committed 51a2df3 on `squidlee/squ-127-stack-27-extract-app-state-into-feature-hooks`, PR #177 draft)**
   - All the feature hooks from the earlier summary.
   - Fix in `src/features/shell/useAppShortcuts.ts`: the deps entry `searchRef.current?.focus,` became `searchRef,`.

   **SQU-128 branch `squidlee/squ-128-stack-37-capture-bar-capture-modal-shortcuts-modal`, uncommitted**

   **`src/ui/Dialog.tsx` (new)**
   ```tsx
   import { Dialog as BaseDialog } from "@base-ui/react/dialog";
   import type { ReactNode, RefObject } from "react";
   import { cx } from "./cx";
   const EASE = "duration-200 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.23,1,0.32,1)]";
   // The viewport fades with the backdrop so the popup's opacity compounds with
   // it, as when the popup sat inside the backdrop.
   const FADE = cx("transition-opacity", EASE, "data-starting-style:opacity-0 data-ending-style:opacity-0");
   export function Dialog({ open, onOpenChange, initialFocus, className, children, ...props }: { open: boolean; onOpenChange: (open: boolean) => void; initialFocus?: RefObject<HTMLElement | null>; className?: string; children: ReactNode; id?: string; }) {
     return (
       <BaseDialog.Root open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}>
         <BaseDialog.Portal>
           <BaseDialog.Backdrop className={cx("fixed inset-0 z-110 bg-[rgba(10,10,9,0.72)]", FADE)} />
           <BaseDialog.Viewport className={cx("fixed inset-0 z-110 grid place-items-center p-6", FADE)}>
             <BaseDialog.Popup initialFocus={initialFocus} className={cx("[transition-property:opacity,transform]", EASE, "data-starting-style:opacity-0 data-starting-style:[transform:translateY(8px)_scale(0.98)] data-ending-style:opacity-0 data-ending-style:[transform:translateY(8px)_scale(0.98)]", className)} {...props}>
               {children}
             </BaseDialog.Popup>
           </BaseDialog.Viewport>
         </BaseDialog.Portal>
       </BaseDialog.Root>
     );
   }
   export const DialogTitle = BaseDialog.Title;
   export const DialogDescription = BaseDialog.Description;
   export const DialogClose = BaseDialog.Close;
   ```

